1
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:20,137
Did you know there's an awesome
treasure hidden at the end of the sea?

2
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:22,857
And anyone who finds it,
the King of the Pirates!

3
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,397
Is that exciting or what?

4
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,127
There are incredible adventures
out there just waiting for us!

5
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:35,320
Bon voyage, have the courage
that sail and believe,

6
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,177
and we will see a glimpse of

7
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,160
the sun rising on our tomorrow.

8
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:50,620
Back when we first started,
we had separate horizons,

9
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,897
sailed toward different dreams.

10
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,297
Things have changed now.

11
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,197
For together we found.

12
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:59,817
We look through the spyglass and see.

13
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,857
And we know.

14
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:05,437
That our hearts have brought us here.

15
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:09,097
Where the conscious points our destiny.

16
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:11,337
There's no looking back.

17
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,977
Take the hell with me.

18
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,097
Bon voyage.

19
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:17,177
We can't stop all our troubles.

20
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,460
Forget the past.

21
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:22,157
Though the future's unclear.

22
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:26,837
Where we still can smile,
we know we'll get there.

23
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,660
No regrets.

24
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:33,720
Every tear that we've cried
only helps our dreams come true.

25
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:39,720
You and those dreams
are precious in my life.

26
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:46,740
A glimpse of the sun
rising on our tomorrow?

27
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:10,900
If you do not wish to be aboard this
ship, there is but one path left for you.

28
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:14,210
Death.

29
00:02:14,293 --> 00:02:15,123
So long.

30
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:21,117
There's no way I can
possibly beat this guy.

31
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:27,297
But I'm not gonna stay on this ship
that's for sure I have no regrets.

32
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:31,877
Yes I know what you're
thinking and by now I'm

33
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,697
sure you realize you
won't be leaving this arc

34
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:39,717
safely that is unless
you're pinning your hopes

35
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:43,420
on those two rats who've
just snuck on board?

36
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,780
Let me off this crazy thing!

37
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:00,900
Sanji, listen!

38
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:03,957
If we go any higher, we
won't be able to get down!

39
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:07,981
Not to mention the fact that God
is on board, or had you forgotten!

40
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,680
We're already here, stupid,
so just deal with it!

41
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,617
But what are we going to do, Sanji?

42
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:16,397
Look at the size of this thing!

43
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,127
I've seen smaller mountains!

44
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,197
There could be hundreds of guys on board!

45
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,692
We can't fight them all!

46
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:26,260
Besides, if God or those
priests are here...

47
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:28,860
Oh, just get over it already.

48
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:32,317
You're the one who's always
prepared for this kind of stuff.

49
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,224
You got all the cool equipment.

50
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,630
Well, this?

51
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,293
Not what I had in mind when I made them!

52
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:43,364
Well, the bad guys have
got that mantra ability.

53
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,897
They can predict our moves.

54
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,477
No point in trying to be sneaky.

55
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:50,397
In fact, I bet my favorite carving
knife they already know we're here.

56
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,715
They know we're here?

57
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,565
So what are we supposed to do?

58
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,944
Stop freaking out for starters.

59
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,437
Once we're safely inside, we'll
split up and head for the main deck.

60
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,960
Nami's got to be up there. Hold on.

61
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:04,580
Did you say split up?

62
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:06,980
Are you out of your mind?

63
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,460
Why would we do that?

64
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,437
We have no idea how many
bad guys are on board.

65
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,617
Just getting up here was dangerous enough.

66
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:14,880
You dumbass.

67
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:19,560
If we don't split up, we could both die.

68
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:21,760
Both die?

69
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:24,215
I don't suppose you care to elaborate.

70
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:26,180
Wait a minute.

71
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:27,917
You're not gonna...

72
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,940
You mean to save Nami?

73
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:33,300
Usopp, listen to me.

74
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:40,040
If it'll save Nami, I'll gladly sacrifice
your life. You jerk! Why are you on it?

75
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,460
All right, then.

76
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,080
I'm coming, Nami!

77
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:44,720
I'm gonna get you!

78
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:59,980
It seems they're quite
serious about your rescue.

79
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,640
Fools to the bitter end!

80
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,420
Who can it be?

81
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:08,860
No one besides Luffy
can still move Besides,

82
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,452
how could they even get on board the Ark?

83
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,120
Though help may have arrived,

84
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:31,520
it doesn't mean you've been saved yet,
nor am I obligated to wait for them.

85
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,820
All I can do is jump overboard
and hope for the best.

86
00:05:36,060 --> 00:05:38,400
If I stay here, I'm dead for sure.

87
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,231
I'm up against lightning.

88
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,780
What else can I do?

89
00:05:56,380 --> 00:05:57,560
What's all this?

90
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,320
There's no one here.

91
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,877
But the ship is huge.

92
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:15,360
Does it run without anyone operating it?

93
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:17,760
And how does it fly anyway?

94
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:20,532
I've never heard of a flying ship before.

95
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,637
Just the thought of being up in the air
like this makes my knees all wobbly.

96
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,661
Oh, I feel sick.

97
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,537
I wonder what the power
source for this thing is.

98
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:29,677
Oh, what do I care?

99
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,936
As long as it doesn't decide to fall.

100
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:34,040
Wait, I just realized.

101
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:37,817
Even if Nami is on the upper deck,
we're way too high up now to jump off.

102
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,665
What the hell are we gonna do?

103
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:09,300
The sky it keeps getting
darker take it up with him.

104
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:18,917
Onto the boat.

105
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,880
Don't get left behind.

106
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,577
Hurry to the white sea.

107
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:25,380
We're running out of time.

108
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,537
Look at it.

109
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:28,561
It's terrifying.

110
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:30,697
This is really it.

111
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:32,120
The end of the world.

112
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,037
Leave the village.

113
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,357
But chief.

114
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,317
What about the warriors.

115
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,694
They're still not back from upper yard.

116
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,800
There is no need to wait.

117
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,740
The chief!

118
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:48,420
We have no choice.

119
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,680
The warriors aren't children.

120
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,880
They can avoid the dangers they face.

121
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,760
Have faith in them.

122
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,060
Enaru will destroy everything.

123
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,900
We know that.

124
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:07,937
Just as he did to his homeland
Birka, so too shall he do here.

125
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,960
We must escape.

126
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:13,840
Now, we must prepare the ships.

127
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,800
Our first task is to save the
lives of the villagers here.

128
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,980
Everything is coming to an end.

129
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:32,020
Wiper, let it go.

130
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:34,560
You've done everything you could.

131
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,460
Did you come from the Blue Sea World?

132
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:44,337
If that's what you call it, we sealed
up a river of clouds to get here.

133
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:46,538
Speaking of here, is this your home?

134
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:50,217
Everything is happening in this
forest right in front of me,

135
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:52,820
and I have no way to know what's going on.

136
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,680
All I can do is wait.

137
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:02,800
Everyone, I hope you're all safe.

138
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,920
Horsie Bird!

139
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,020
Horsie Bird, I'm sorry!

140
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,065
You were trying to protect me!

141
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:26,477
Aisa!

142
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:27,457
Aisa!

143
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:28,520
Aisa!

144
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,560
Luffy?

145
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,120
Are you alive?

146
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:33,060
Over here!

147
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:34,660
This way!

148
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,100
Hey! I saw!

149
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:39,370
Hey!

150
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,460
Help me out!

151
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,480
How did you land like that?

152
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,760
Alright! Dammit!

153
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:57,377
I can't get this golden ball off!

154
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:58,754
Hey, watch your mouth!

155
00:09:58,980 --> 00:10:02,180
Let's just get back to that
beanstalk where Robin was!

156
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:04,576
I won't let Eneru get away with this!

157
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:09,597
Okay, nice try, jerk, but it
takes a lot more to stop me.

158
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:13,360
Your arcs toast, and I know
just where to find you?

159
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,457
Congratulations, young lady!

160
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,600
That was rather amusing!

161
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,777
I did it!

162
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:43,820
Such clever toys you have
down on the Blue Sea.

163
00:10:47,760 --> 00:10:48,600
Thunderbolt!

164
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:58,180
Creating a path for the
lightning to follow.

165
00:10:58,580 --> 00:10:59,880
A clever tactic.

166
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:03,654
You're obviously well acquainted
with weather phenomena.

167
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:07,400
But it's not enough.

168
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,980
You realize, of course, it's futile.

169
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:17,780
All I need do is raise the voltage
and your trick won't work, will it?

170
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:21,420
Now I'm a very busy man.

171
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:23,050
Begone!

172
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,480
Can't dodge this one!

173
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,160
Why don't you be gone?

174
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:30,640
Exploding star!

175
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:44,200
Oops, I'm sorry.

176
00:11:45,020 --> 00:11:45,850
Usopp?

177
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:47,760
I know you.

178
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,300
From the ship.

179
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:54,740
Hey, where's Sanji? Sanji?

180
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:55,820
He's here too?

181
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,100
You mean he's not up here yet?

182
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,280
I see.

183
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:06,710
Later!

184
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,220
Can't see!

185
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:18,220
Be a man, Usopp.

186
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,911
What are you running for?

187
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:22,460
Bring it on, God!

188
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:31,670
Usopp!

189
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,900
Nami! Yeah, what?

190
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,940
Tell me what to do, I'm on it!

191
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,437
Please save me!

192
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,597
What the hell?!

193
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:43,857
I thought you came here to
save me, you spineless chicken!

194
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:47,160
Yeah, um, I'm not really
sure what's going on anymore.

195
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,017
Then what are you doing here?!

196
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,580
Well... Well, what?

197
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:53,327
Get your rear-end gear
and save me right now!

198
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,820
How do I do that exactly?

199
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,340
We are fighting God. Oh, yeah.

200
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:09,460
By the way, Ami, about that hat.

201
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:10,920
Yeah, it's Luffy's.

202
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:14,377
He was here a little while ago,
but Eneru threw him overboard.

203
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,580
But he's not dead, I'm sure of it.

204
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,657
The arc's gaining altitude.

205
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:20,617
We can't count on Luffy to save us.

206
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:21,530
Right.

207
00:13:21,613 --> 00:13:25,026
We've got to do this ourselves,
because I'm not a fan of dying.

208
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:26,280
I'm with you now!

209
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:36,580
Here, come hide behind this tube thingy.

210
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:41,056
I'm betting it's pretty important,
so he might not use his big attacks.

211
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,073
Usopp, look over there!

212
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:46,020
A waver!

213
00:13:46,280 --> 00:13:48,104
We'll have to jump off on that!

214
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,920
Jump from this height? Are you nuts?

215
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,200
No, look!

216
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:55,197
There's a patch of island cloud
in the middle of the forest!

217
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:57,920
If we can reach that,
we just might make it!

218
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,520
Of course!

219
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:03,740
Damn it!

220
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:18,660
I'll go try to create a
diversion. Get it ready. Right!

221
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,060
Take this, guard!

222
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:22,850
Behold!

223
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,760
Usopp's spell!

224
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:30,540
A splinter embeds itself
deep under your fingernail.

225
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:34,260
That hurts just thinking about it.

226
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:36,097
Cover your ears, you idiot!

227
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,592
This stuff can kill you!

228
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:42,140
A piece of paper cuts across
the skin of your knuckles.

229
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:49,020
Five kankersaurs inflaming your gums!

230
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:55,100
Usopp, no!

231
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,026
Gotta get this thing running.

232
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:02,651
We're only gonna get one chance to escape.

233
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:07,660
Hang on.

234
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:15,660
Looks good.

235
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:18,457
The island cloud is directly
below that beanstalk.

236
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,370
Look!

237
00:15:19,453 --> 00:15:20,283
I'm ready!

238
00:15:20,366 --> 00:15:21,196
Let's get...

239
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:27,970
Usa!

240
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:35,280
Though you may desperately
want to run away,

241
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,840
facing me, it will not be that simple.

242
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,440
But please, do try it again.

243
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,820
I always enjoy a deadly game of Tang.

244
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:00,400
Usopp, grab my hand!

245
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,750
Come on!

246
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:07,840
I'm dead!

247
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:18,560
For you, there is no hope of salvation.

248
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:22,550
Usopp!

249
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:33,140
Get going.

250
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,760
Sanji, run!

251
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,780
Got it, Nami!

252
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:40,390
Pour!

253
00:16:47,780 --> 00:16:48,980
Uso, wait!

254
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,261
Let off the gas!

255
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:51,250
What about Sanji?

256
00:16:51,333 --> 00:16:53,000
Don't stop! We gotta escape!

257
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,580
Now stop making my plans sound bad!

258
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:57,100
And keep going!

259
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,120
So they jumped.

260
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:15,960
Do they still not understand
the range of my powers?

261
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:19,040
They haven't escaped me in the slightest.

262
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:31,020
Hey, God, there's something I
wanted to tell you, but first,

263
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:36,300
I should thank you.

264
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:44,177
I was looking for a light.

265
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:45,280
Appreciate it.

266
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:48,610
Right.

267
00:17:48,693 --> 00:17:50,140
Do you have a point?

268
00:17:52,140 --> 00:17:52,970
Yeah.

269
00:17:53,053 --> 00:17:53,883
Get ready...

270
00:17:53,966 --> 00:17:56,120
to cry, bastard.

271
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:09,000
What?

272
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,460
My Ark!

273
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:33,557
Get ready to cry bastard?

274
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,820
Damn you!

275
00:18:38,180 --> 00:18:40,197
You did something below deck?

276
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,800
What have you done to my ark?

277
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:49,157
You fool, you wretched fool!

278
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:52,017
The gears have gone awry!

279
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:54,320
I must fix them.

280
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,060
Don't you worry.

281
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:21,432
Nami fell safely into some island clouds.

282
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,310
Usa?

283
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,270
Hoppy!

284
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,480
Oh, no!

285
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:39,657
We're gonna crash!

286
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:42,269
We're gonna crash and
then we're gonna die!

287
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,270
AHHHHHHHHHHH!

288
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,620
Dosak! Sanji!

289
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:59,240
Rami, is that you?

290
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:01,377
Sounds like you made it down alright.

291
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,290
What a relief.

292
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:05,357
Sanji, you are a real
- Sanji, are you okay?

293
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,280
You got burnt to a crisp rust.

294
00:20:07,420 --> 00:20:08,360
I'm so sorry.

295
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,637
I promise I'll make it up to you somehow.

296
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,780
Hey, I can't breathe!

297
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:15,020
I can't breathe! Nami! Sorry!

298
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:16,437
Hurry up and pull me out!

299
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,350
I can't breathe!

300
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,040
Oh, sorry. All right.

301
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,644
Let's get the heck out of here!

302
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,300
Curse you, Blue Sea Dweller.

303
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:46,540
This vessel is not so easily brought down.

304
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:50,720
I am fully acquainted with
the Ark's drive circuits.

305
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:54,860
We may lack electricity,

306
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,717
but a backup system
harnesses the wind power of

307
00:20:57,800 --> 00:21:01,200
200 jet dials I gathered
in my homeland of Biennale.

308
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:07,440
They will keep this ship
aloft for quite some time.

309
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:12,460
No matter what you feeble beings try...

310
00:21:22,860 --> 00:21:27,160
This land and all its pathetic
inhabitants will perish.

311
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:32,340
Okay, guys, check out that huge vine.

312
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:35,277
If it's the same one I saw
when I was down in the ruins,

313
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:39,397
then it stands to reason we're on
the island clouds right above them.

314
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:40,310
Ruins?

315
00:21:40,393 --> 00:21:43,500
Oh, the City of Gold!
It's real? It's real.

316
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:46,955
But Enoru took all the gold
that was there for himself.

317
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:51,298
If the ruins are beneath us, Zoro
and the others should be down there.

318
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:54,079
I may not know the lay of the land.

319
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,220
But I do know one thing.

320
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,929
Staying here is dangerous.

321
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,240
You got that right. Hop on!

322
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:05,277
Let's find everyone and
get off this island!

323
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:06,480
That's a plan.

324
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:12,000
There are no safe places left in Skypiea.

325
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,660
Luffy, look out!

326
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:40,220
No!

327
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,040
Wait, Luffy!

328
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:46,300
That's the wrong way! Go left! Left!

329
00:22:47,340 --> 00:22:50,680
There's no way I can turn that shark!

330
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,680
Gum-gum-pum!

331
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:07,256
Stop destroying my homeland!

332
00:23:07,339 --> 00:23:08,169
Giant Jack is over that-a-way!

333
00:23:08,252 --> 00:23:09,457
I know, but...

334
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:11,820
Stop breaking things!

335
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:13,720
Stop it!

336
00:23:18,260 --> 00:23:19,380
Oh, man.

337
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:21,905
Robin and the others are gone.

338
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:23,360
Zoro and Chopper.

339
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:25,700
And Wiper and Gonefall.

340
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:28,940
I'm guessing they must
have climbed up already.

341
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:32,280
Yeah, Robin must have
helped them. Let's go.

342
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:36,680
Hey, Aisa!

343
00:23:41,900 --> 00:23:46,440
Will the Sky Islands really be destroyed?

344
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:08,953
Wait for in the others.

345
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:10,708
They're right through here.

346
00:24:17,780 --> 00:24:20,956
I suspect the ship is moving
towards the Grand Belfry.

347
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:23,797
Wonder what happened to
Miss Navigator and the boys.

348
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:27,480
If they're on that ship,
it could mean they're...

349
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:32,300
We're through!

350
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,210
Ah!

351
00:24:38,293 --> 00:24:40,920
Luffy down there! Stop! Stop!

352
00:24:41,780 --> 00:24:42,610
Robin!

353
00:24:43,180 --> 00:24:44,298
What are you doing?

354
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:47,000
Look after these two for me!

355
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:00,746
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, stop!

356
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,070
Luffy.

357
00:25:04,660 --> 00:25:06,400
You grew extra hands!

358
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,765
What have you got on your arm?

359
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:13,100
Robin, the golden bell is at
the top of this vine, right?

360
00:25:13,740 --> 00:25:16,920
And Enneru is trying to get
his hands on it, isn't he?

361
00:25:17,660 --> 00:25:18,490
That's right.

362
00:25:18,580 --> 00:25:21,933
If the Grand Balfry exists,
then the bell would be there.

363
00:25:22,380 --> 00:25:23,920
But he's already good!

364
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:27,130
Loopy!

365
00:25:28,480 --> 00:25:32,317
So, young lady, have
you seen our navigator?

366
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:34,900
A woman with orange hair. You mean Nami?

367
00:25:35,060 --> 00:25:36,119
She's on the ship.

368
00:25:39,220 --> 00:25:41,960
I only hear one voice coming from the sky.

369
00:25:47,340 --> 00:25:48,400
Here they are!

370
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,600
Oh, Robin!

371
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:57,661
Miss Navigator, with long
nose, and the cook, too.

372
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:00,790
Isa!

373
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:04,680
Thank goodness, you all right? Nami!

374
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:07,870
Huh?

375
00:26:07,953 --> 00:26:11,920
Zoro, Chopper, weird
old guy, and a gorilla.

376
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:15,740
Oh, everyone's been taken down.

377
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:18,520
Oh, if only I had been here.

378
00:26:18,740 --> 00:26:20,211
Wait, Isa, where's Luffy?

379
00:26:20,340 --> 00:26:21,337
Wasn't he with you?

380
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:23,880
Luffy climbed up the vine to rescue you.

381
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:27,948
But since everyone's here, Luffy
has to face Inru by himself.

382
00:26:29,060 --> 00:26:31,780
We missed him, didn't we? Just now.

383
00:26:32,040 --> 00:26:34,657
I tried to stop him,
but he wouldn't lose me.

384
00:26:34,740 --> 00:26:35,622
Damn it, Luffy!

385
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:38,576
He knows we're running short on time.

386
00:26:38,700 --> 00:26:39,800
We gotta go now!

387
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:41,940
Go on without me.

388
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:44,040
I'll take the waiver and find him.

389
00:26:44,660 --> 00:26:46,778
Just try to get to the Mary somehow.

390
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:52,520
Oh, man!

391
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,480
That ship is moving fast!

392
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:58,000
In a row!

393
00:27:02,060 --> 00:27:03,600
Quickly, get on the ships!

394
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:05,605
The whole sky's turning black!

395
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,320
What's wrong?

396
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:15,300
We need to flee at once.

397
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:16,500
My daughter, Isa.

398
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:17,897
She still hasn't...

399
00:27:17,980 --> 00:27:19,745
Ah, she still hasn't returned.

400
00:27:20,220 --> 00:27:21,840
Isa is a bright child.

401
00:27:22,380 --> 00:27:26,674
We must have faith that she is with
some warriors and we'll be protected.

402
00:27:32,360 --> 00:27:35,007
The thunderclouds are
gushing out nicely now.

403
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:46,240
Hurry! Hurry up!

404
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:51,057
Captain, if we don't use the boats at
the dock, we'll never fit everyone in.

405
00:27:51,140 --> 00:27:53,037
They'd have to sail all the way around.

406
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:57,140
You men, use styles to create
rivers inside the island at once.

407
00:27:57,300 --> 00:28:00,300
How many of the islanders are left?

408
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:01,760
Almost half of them.

409
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:03,460
People only.

410
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:04,640
No more baggage.

411
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:08,400
And get everybody out to
sea right away. Yes, sir.

412
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:18,180
Hold it.

413
00:28:18,740 --> 00:28:23,037
Nobody's leaving until everyone pays
the $2 billion ex-toll departure fee.

414
00:28:23,120 --> 00:28:24,580
Amazon, hurry!

415
00:28:24,800 --> 00:28:26,980
You can still escape with us! Huh?

416
00:28:27,340 --> 00:28:29,740
Hurry to Cloud End! Huh?

417
00:28:29,980 --> 00:28:31,120
The Sky Islands...

418
00:28:31,800 --> 00:28:32,630
Huh?

419
00:28:32,713 --> 00:28:33,926
...are about to be destroyed!

420
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:37,850
Oh...

421
00:28:38,780 --> 00:28:39,610
Bye...

422
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:56,380
The wind has stopped.

423
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:20,580
Run! Run!

424
00:29:31,620 --> 00:29:36,920
Now then, let us begin the festivities.

425
00:29:38,740 --> 00:29:41,180
The time for endings has come.

426
00:29:49,520 --> 00:29:50,350
Mamaragon.

427
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:03,520
Get away from the island! Run!

428
00:30:06,220 --> 00:30:08,279
The lightning keeps getting bigger!

429
00:30:08,520 --> 00:30:10,937
The boats at the docks
have been destroyed!

430
00:30:11,020 --> 00:30:12,777
To the western end of the beach!

431
00:30:12,860 --> 00:30:13,690
Quickly!

432
00:30:13,840 --> 00:30:15,277
There's still boats there!

433
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,301
Run to the west!

434
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:17,580
Move people!

435
00:30:17,940 --> 00:30:19,234
Leave your belongings!

436
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:31,300
Chief, we need to get you on a boat.

437
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:40,860
Great warrior Kalgara, I
beg you, protect us all.

438
00:30:56,360 --> 00:30:58,640
Man, those lightning bolts are huge!

439
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:01,548
We're gonna end up Sky
Dust if we stay here!

440
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,540
Guys, go now!

441
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:09,497
Once I find Bloopie,
we'll be right behind you!

442
00:31:09,580 --> 00:31:11,280
Uh, yeah, right. I gotcha.

443
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:18,930
Hurry, Robin.

444
00:31:19,013 --> 00:31:21,979
We gotta find a way to carry
these guys to the ship.

445
00:31:22,300 --> 00:31:23,130
Wiper!

446
00:31:32,020 --> 00:31:32,850
Swordsman.

447
00:31:34,220 --> 00:31:35,340
Weird old guy!

448
00:31:35,740 --> 00:31:37,480
Oh good, you're awake now.

449
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:39,117
There's not a moment to lose.

450
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:40,965
Do you think you can walk yet?

451
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:42,270
So...

452
00:31:42,353 --> 00:31:43,520
Energo has begun.

453
00:31:49,780 --> 00:31:51,380
We must all hurry now.

454
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:54,229
There is truly nothing
more we can do here.

455
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:00,030
Viper...

456
00:32:04,080 --> 00:32:05,668
We have to get out of here!

457
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:08,565
Not even Luffy can handle
an enemy who can fly!

458
00:32:08,780 --> 00:32:12,015
I have to get to him before
this island is obliterated!

459
00:32:23,140 --> 00:32:23,970
Magnificent!

460
00:32:25,580 --> 00:32:27,897
You better not think for a second that I'm

461
00:32:27,980 --> 00:32:30,451
gonna let you get away with this in a row!

462
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:38,440
When you're lost and alone,
I can always hear your voice.

463
00:32:38,960 --> 00:32:43,537
While you wander far from
home, gazing up at the sky.

464
00:32:43,620 --> 00:32:46,380
You are just like the moon,

465
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:50,880
you never change as you
climb into the night.

466
00:32:54,480 --> 00:32:57,860
But your reflection wanes,

467
00:32:58,200 --> 00:33:02,137
then you disappear fading so silently.

468
00:33:02,220 --> 00:33:06,057
Stay as you are.

469
00:33:06,140 --> 00:33:08,657
Don't lose your way.

470
00:33:08,740 --> 00:33:11,860
Let these words guide you.

471
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:15,900
Don't ever look back.

472
00:33:17,820 --> 00:33:21,177
Don't give up on your dreams.

473
00:33:21,260 --> 00:33:22,517
They're windless nights.

474
00:33:22,600 --> 00:33:26,577
They come to you again and again.

475
00:33:26,660 --> 00:33:29,257
Until you see the journey through.

476
00:33:29,340 --> 00:33:35,237
You may not return, I
hope that you'll learn.

477
00:33:35,320 --> 00:33:40,680
To put your past behind,
and just keep moving on.
